 ## v0.28.2 Android SQLite open fix
 The v0.28.1 recovery surface exposed the next real-device blocker: Android sqflite rejects `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` through `execute()` because that PRAGMA returns data. v0.28.2 keeps the visible startup recovery and performs query-returning PRAGMAs through `rawQuery()`.
+
+
+## v0.28.3 real-device fixes
+The Android 15 checkpoint exposed two independent issues: AGP release stripping changed the user-validated `libbertvits2.so` fingerprint, and chat startup awaited best-effort long-running maintenance before exposing the message list. v0.28.3 preserves the six Meju native payloads during release packaging, fixes daily-continuity maintenance allowlisting, moves startup maintenance off the visible chat loading path, and adds a small on-device DeepSeek API connection probe.
